<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95116" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπ-ιάζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιά</span>)
		poet. Verb, almost always pres. and impf., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spy from a high place</i> or
				<i>watch-tower</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				2.6
			</span></i>: generally, <i>spy, watch</i>, even on a plain, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.260
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>watch for shoals of fish</i>, applied to certain members of a
			guild of lsis-worshippers, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				1.817.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Callipolis</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans., <i>spy out, watch</i>, c.acc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.606
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, <i>look out for, watch</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼς θύννως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					3.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.918
				</span></i>
			, etc.: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιασάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Callicrat.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.28.18
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
